{"Workspace":"/Users/workspace/Workspace/captn","ObservationCache":{"7dc55e86a8a039d8:597e4f9d9fda4c3c:f5e3c6746de7c564:1fb1e4892b9e10e3":{"id":"s1","behavior":"Implements the `COG` type: a workspace-scoped container holding a graph of `COGNode` polymorphic nodes keyed by `common.HashType`, with caches for loaded/loading files and observation results, protected by a mutex. `OpenCOG`/`Persist` read and write `captn.cog` as JSON. `LoadFile` deduplicates concurrent parses via a `loadFileCall` channel pattern, then parses and adds a vertex with an `import_type` attribute. `LoadFiles` parallelizes via `common.ParallelCollect`. `QuerySnippet` finds the snippet range in a file, collects child AST nodes, identifies call-expression symbols, batches LSP definition lookups, resolves dependencies, preloads dependency files, links each external dependency node to the nearest node-of-interest in the source, builds an `ObservationGraph` with the module as root and adds edges from root or chain ancestors to each interest node. `queryWithDepth`/`QueryWithDepth` recursively expand a node's dependencies up to a depth, skipping standard-library and package imports, using a visited set and mutex with `wg.Go` for concurrency. `IsNodeOfInterest` returns true only for `*ast.ASTBlock`."},"9a71f0629bda6bdf:0000000000000000:0000000000000000:0000000000000000":{"id":"c1","behavior":"Represents the main run case (s2) invoking `g.QuerySnippet(ctx, cli.Args[1], cli.Args[2])` to obtain an observation graph for the requested snippet."},"af6c4e57190e79fd:088ca19bddf873b7:e4785da5797d095f:5e8e62e02d84bcf7":{"id":"s0","behavior":"Defines a Kong-based CLI with a `run \u003cpath\u003e \u003csnippet\u003e` command. When invoked, it starts a runtime/trace recording to `trace.out`, opens a COG at the current working directory, instantiates a Claude Code provider, calls `QuerySnippet` to obtain an observation graph and start node, invokes `ExplainWithDepth` with depth 1, prints the explanation, and persists the COG. Errors panic; trace task `loadCOG` brackets the COG open."},"bdb1395c6439e7f4:b9a642fcd5035847:8c8042d0e7533edf:c0844a48392406c6":{"id":"s2","behavior":"The body of the `main` switch case (same logic as s0's main): parses CLI args, sets up runtime/trace output, opens the COG at cwd inside a `loadCOG` trace task, creates a Claude Code provider, queries the snippet, explains it with depth 1, prints the result, and persists the COG."},"da7780715cc67c19:0000000000000000:0000000000000000:0000000000000000":{"id":"c0","behavior":"Represents the main run case (s2) invoking `cog.OpenCOG(cwd)` to load the COG from the workspace."}}}